C1       N4 IS CORRECTED: the distinction is NOT A6 alone
         N4 concluded: 'd = 3 is the unique field ramified only at 3 AND has the
         smallest |D| -- those are ONE fact, and it is MINIMALITY, i.e. A6 restated.'
         THE 'ONE FACT' STEP DOES NOT FOLLOW, and it is this seat's overreach.
         fields with a PRIME discriminant (ramified at ONE prime): d = [1, 2, 3, 7, 11, 19, 23, 31, 43, 47]
           -> 'ramified at a single prime' is a property MANY fields have;
              'ramified only at 3' picks one, and 'minimal |D|' picks one, and
              THEY ARE DIFFERENT PROPERTIES THAT HAPPEN TO COINCIDE AT d = 3.
           -> |D| = 3 is minimal because a fundamental discriminant is 0 or 1 mod 4,
              so -1 and -2 are excluded and -3 is the first -- a CONGRUENCE fact,
              NOT a consequence of '3 is the only ramified prime'.

         THE HONEST DECOMPOSITION, which ADDENDUM 1's A4 makes visible:
           fields with |O^x| > 2: d = [1, 3]  -- and those are EXACTLY the two
           imaginary quadratic fields that are CYCLOTOMIC: Q(zeta_4) and Q(zeta_3).
           Being cyclotomic is what supplies mu_6, hence the cusp's Z/3 (A4).
           It leaves TWO candidates; MINIMALITY (A6) picks Q(zeta_3) between them.
         => d = 3 IS SELECTED BY: CYCLOTOMIC (an arithmetic fact A6 does NOT supply)
            PLUS A6.  N4 said 'A6 restated'.  THAT WAS TOO STRONG: one bit of the
            selection is genuinely arithmetic, and xB017 gave it away.
C1 PASS  N4 CORRECTED.  d = 3 is MORE distinguished than xB017 said,
